WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:14.900
Jack the Ripper: The Killer from Hell

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:20.890
“Dear Boss,
Grand work the last job was.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.140
I gave the lady no time to squeal.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.449
How can they catch me now.

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:27.230
I love my work and want to start again.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:32.929
You will soon hear of me with my funny little
games...My knife's so nice and sharp I want

00:00:32.929 --> 00:00:36.510
to get to work right away if I get a chance.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.670
Good Luck.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.510
Yours truly,
Jack the Ripper”

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:44.719
Those were extracts from a letter that London’s
Central News Agency received on September

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:46.179
27, 1888.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:50.780
It was then forwarded to Scotland Yard who
were in the middle of investigating, perhaps,

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.440
the most notorious killing spree of all time.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.619
Someone was attacking women in Whitechapel,
murdering them and then cutting up their bodies

00:00:58.619 --> 00:01:00.179
in gruesome fashion.

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:04.839
The killer went by many names - the Whitechapel
Murderer, Leather Apron, Saucy Jacky, and,

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:07.030
of course, Jack the Ripper.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:12.469
He remains unidentified to this day so we
will focus on his grim body of work - the

00:01:12.469 --> 00:01:15.189
murders, the suspects, the investigations.

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:20.049
Few, if any other killers in history have
inspired so many studies, books, and hypotheses

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:27.240
courtesy of police officers, historians, writers,
and crime buffs who are collectively known

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.240
as ripperologists.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.420
Today we explore the life of Jack the Ripper.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:42.250
The Autumn of Terror Begins - Mary Ann Nichols
In 1888, the Whitechapel parish in the East

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.319
End of London was a place rife with crime.

00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:50.939
It was an overcrowded low-income area with
terrible housing and working conditions.

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:55.469
There was a brothel on every corner and a
bar next to every brothel so the residents

00:01:55.469 --> 00:01:59.530
may indulge their vices and forget about their
poverty-stricken lives.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:04.850
But even for such an area, nobody was prepared
for what they were about to discover one early

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.920
morning on August 31.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:11.319
A man named Charles Cross was on his way to
his job on Buck’s Row.

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:16.069
On the way, he found a woman lying prone in
the street, with her skirt raised above her

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.069
waist.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:21.180
Cross and another man named Robert Paul approached
her and touched her head and hands, unable

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.020
to decide if she was dead or merely unconscious.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:28.010
The two concluded that they should pull down
her skirt and that they would alert the first

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:32.540
police officer they encountered but, otherwise,
they had jobs to get to.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.519
The streets of Whitechapel were poorly lit
and it was still night outside.

00:02:36.519 --> 00:02:40.790
In the darkness, even up-close, neither man
noticed that the woman’s throat had been

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.260
slit and her abdomen mutilated.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:48.640
A police constable named John Neil came upon
the body, followed closely by Constable Mizen

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.739
who had been alerted by Cross.

00:02:50.739 --> 00:02:52.860
A third constable went to fetch the doctor.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.450
The physician pronounced the woman dead and
concluded that she had been killed about half

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:57.459
an hour prior.

00:02:57.459 --> 00:03:02.380
This meant that the killer was, likely, still
in the area when Charles Cross walked by.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:06.500
The victim was Mary Ann Nichols, a prostitute
who also went by “Polly”.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:11.599
At first, her murder was linked to a few other
killings which we will talk about a bit later.

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:15.939
While some blamed a violent gang, the newspapers
ran with the story of one deranged killer

00:03:15.939 --> 00:03:17.349
preying on these women.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:21.629
In the weeks that followed, street gossip
created the belief that the killer was a local

00:03:21.629 --> 00:03:24.150
Jewish man known as “Leather Apron.”

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:28.390
Whitechapel had a large Jewish population
so resentment against them was high.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:32.650
Of course, the newspapers were more than happy
to fuel this sensationalism.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:37.180
Whether it was due to frustration, incompetence,
or outside pressure to do something, the police

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.269
decided to arrest John Pizer in September.

00:03:40.269 --> 00:03:44.810
He was a Polish Jew who worked as a shoemaker
and some said that he was sometimes called

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:45.810
“Leather Apron.”

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.760
He also had a prior conviction for a stabbing
attack.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:53.030
This was all the police had against Pizer
but, fortunately for him, he had a solid alibi

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.550
that exculpated him.

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:59.319
Pizer even won a libel case against a newspaper
that declared him to be the killer.

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:06.940
The Second Murder - Annie Chapman
On September 8, the Whitechapel Murderer struck

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:11.680
again when the body of Annie Chapman was found
in the backyard of Danbury Street by an elderly

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.680
resident.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.269
He flagged down some passing workmen who alerted
the police.

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:19.830
Chapman’s throat had a deep cut and her
body had been mutilated with multiple stab

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:24.010
wounds, immediately suggesting a connection
with the murder of Mary Nichols.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:29.040
She had been disemboweled and her intestines
had been severed, lifted out of the body and

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.090
placed on her shoulder.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:34.790
A later post-mortem examination revealed that
the killer had removed and taken Chapman’s

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:35.790
uterus.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:40.080
Dr. George Bagster Phillips examined the wounds
and ascertained that they were caused by a

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.810
very sharp knife with a long, thin, and narrow
blade.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:48.350
It could have been the surgical instrument
that a doctor might use for a post-mortem.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:53.280
Phillips also said in his testimony that the
murderer showed “indications of anatomical

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.280
knowledge.”

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:58.190
These conclusions gave birth to the idea that
the killer might be someone with a medical

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:01.160
background, a notion that is still pervasive
today.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:05.650
The murders caused a huge sensation in London
and were discussed in every newspaper in the

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:06.650
city.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:10.980
Meanwhile, the police had to contend with
an unexpected problem that significantly impeded

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:13.300
their already-plodding investigation.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.210
They had to look into hundreds of letters
received from the public.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:21.780
Broadly, these missives could be placed into
two categories: letters from people offering

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:26.810
suggestions or information on how to catch
the culprit and letters alleged to be from

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:27.930
the killer himself.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.300
The police received upwards of 700 letters
from the public.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:36.380
Hundreds were purportedly from the Whitechapel
Murderer, either taunting or expressing remorse

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:37.380
for his actions.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.380
You might imagine how this made it almost
impossible for the police to ascertain which

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.380
of the letters, if any, were useful or genuine.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:42.090
That being said, there are a few which are
believed by many investigators to have some

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.090
merit.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:45.770
The first one we mentioned in the intro of
the video.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:50.470
It was sent to the Central News Agency almost
20 days after the murder of Annie Chapman.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:55.150
It starts with the words “Dear Boss” and
ends with the murderer giving himself a name.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.080
From now on, he is known as Jack the Ripper.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:03.360
The Double Event - Catherine Eddowes and Elizabeth
Stride

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:08.060
At first, the “Dear Boss” letter was dismissed
as a hoax like all the others.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:11.650
However, one particular phrase garnered the
interest of the police.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:15.710
When talking about his next job, Jack said
that he will “clip the ladys ears off.”

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:19.740
This became relevant when, just a few days
later, the killer did just that.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:24.450
On September 30, two women fell victim to
the Ripper: Elizabeth Stride and Catherine

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.460
Eddowes.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:28.560
First off was Elizabeth Stride, also known
as “Long Liz”.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:32.070
She was last seen around midnight in the company
of an unidentified man.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:37.210
She was killed soon after that and her body
had already been discovered by 1 a.m. at Dutfield’s

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:38.820
Yard on Berner Street.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:43.920
Liz died from a long, six-inch gash in her
neck, but had suffered no mutilations.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.710
Because of this, some are still reticent to
count her as a Ripper victim, believing that

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:50.810
she could have been the target of an unrelated
attack.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:55.290
However, others consider that there are enough
similarities such as location and killing

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:57.640
method to group her with the other women.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:01.310
They believe that Jack did not cut up her
body because he was either rushing to kill

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:04.270
again or, perhaps, because he was interrupted.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:08.560
This is where a Hungarian Jew named Israel
Schwartz came in with an interesting story

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:12.680
to share which, if true, meant that he might
have been the interrupter.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:17.690
Schwartz told police that he saw a man assault
a woman on Berner Street at around 12:45 a.m.

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:18.780
that night.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:22.530
Believing he was witnessing a domestic spat
between husband and wife, he wanted nothing

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:24.760
to do with it and crossed the street to avoid
them.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:28.110
He later identified Long Liz as the woman
he saw that night.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:33.620
His cowardice was subsequently mocked in newspapers
which labelled Schwartz a “hen-hearted creature.”

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:36.770
There are two peculiar details about his story.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:41.851
Firstly, Schwartz claimed that there was a
second man in the vicinity smoking a pipe.

00:07:41.851 --> 00:07:45.450
Secondly, the witness said that the attacker
saw him and shouted something at him.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:50.530
Schwartz believed the word was “Lipski”,
an anti-semitic slur which referenced Israel

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.690
Lipski, a Jewish man hanged for murder the
year before.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:58.420
We don’t know how serious police took Schwartz’s
account, but they did not call on him to testify

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.420
at the inquest.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:04.300
Their records do indicate that they tracked
down and eliminated the second man as a suspect.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:08.630
Meanwhile, within walking distance of Berner
Street, Jack had found himself another victim

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:10.570
named Catherine “Kate” Eddowes.

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:14.880
After midnight, Kate was walking the streets
of London after being released from jail for

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:16.050
drunken behavior.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:20.910
She ended up in Mitre Square and was last
seen alive at around 1:30 a.m. in the company

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:24.840
of a man by three Jewish gentlemen leaving
a club on Duke Street.

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:28.940
One of those three, Joseph Lawende, got a
decent look at the couple and described them,

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.410
although he mainly remembered their clothes
and not their features.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:35.909
Eddowes body was discovered soon after by
a constable walking his beat.

00:08:35.909 --> 00:08:41.180
Her neck had been cut and her body suffered
gruesome mutilations, more extensive than

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:42.409
any of the previous victims.

00:08:42.409 --> 00:08:46.030
Her face was disfigured, her intestines were
removed and placed on her shoulder again,

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:49.830
and the killer had removed her left kidney
and part of her uterus.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:54.180
Jack had also cut off Kate’s right ear which
is what convinced authorities that the “Dear

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.820
Boss” letter was the genuine article.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:10:31.240
More Letters Arrive
Speaking of letters, the next day the Central

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:33.269
News Agency received a postcard.

00:10:33.269 --> 00:10:36.600
The text said:
“I was not codding dear old Boss when I

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:41.649
gave you the tip, you'll hear about Saucy
Jacky's work tomorrow double event this time

00:10:41.649 --> 00:10:45.379
number one squealed a bit couldn't finish
straight off.

00:10:45.379 --> 00:10:49.750
Had not time to get ears off for police thanks
for keeping last letter back till I got to

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.899
work again.

00:10:50.899 --> 00:10:53.529
Jack the Ripper”
The details and the handwriting suggested

00:10:53.529 --> 00:10:58.579
to police not only that the postcard was real,
but that it was written by the same person

00:10:58.579 --> 00:11:00.490
as the “Dear Boss” letter.

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:05.630
They published a facsimile in the hope that
someone might recognize the handwriting, but

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:06.720
were unsuccessful.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.990
Unfortunately, while it is true that both
were probably written by the same person,

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:14.269
it is also possible that that person was not
Jack the Ripper.

00:11:14.269 --> 00:11:18.529
Since the start, some investigators believed
that these letters were the work of journalists,

00:11:18.529 --> 00:11:21.269
specifically either Fred Best or Thomas Bulling.

00:11:21.269 --> 00:11:25.279
They had access to confidential information
and wanted to keep interest in Jack alive.

00:11:25.279 --> 00:11:29.660
Indeed, it is quite feasible that all the
correspondence purported to be from Jack the

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:34.430
Ripper was actually written by other people
who wanted to be part of the sick charade

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:36.040
that surrounded the murders.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:41.160
One more letter merits inclusion, though,
because it came with a grisly accessory - part

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.430
of a human kidney.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:47.089
This missive was addressed “From Hell”
and was sent to George Lusk, chairman of a

00:11:47.089 --> 00:11:51.100
volunteer vigilante group called the Whitechapel
Vigilance Committee.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.870
It read:
“Mr Lusk,

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.370
Sir
I send you half the Kidney I took from one

00:11:55.370 --> 00:12:00.079
women preserved it for you tother piece I
fried and ate it was very nice.

00:12:00.079 --> 00:12:05.610
I may send you the bloody knife that took
it out if you only wate a while longer

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:09.110
signed
Catch me when you can Mishter Lusk”

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:13.149
The handwriting in this letter was definitely
not the same as the first two.

00:12:13.149 --> 00:12:17.980
Obviously, the implication was that the kidney
belonged to the fourth victim, Catherine Eddowes.

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:22.579
Dr. Thomas Openshaw of the London Hospital
examined the organ and concluded that it was,

00:12:22.579 --> 00:12:23.600
indeed, human.

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:28.259
Subsequently, Openshaw received his own Ripper
letter where Jack lamented that “coppers

00:12:28.259 --> 00:12:32.699
spoilt the game” and foiled his attempt
to claim another victim near Openshaw’s

00:12:32.699 --> 00:12:33.699
hospital.

00:12:33.699 --> 00:12:41.500
The Final Victim - Mary Jane Kelly
Jack the Ripper saved his most vicious kill

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.509
for last.

00:12:42.509 --> 00:12:47.759
His victim was Mary Jane Kelly, an Irish working
girl who, at only 25 years old, was much younger

00:12:47.759 --> 00:12:49.440
than the other murdered women.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:53.290
Also unlike the rest, she was killed in her
home rather than on the street.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:57.449
Kelly’s body was discovered on the morning
of November 9 at her lodging at 13 Miller’s

00:12:57.449 --> 00:13:00.480
Court by Thomas Bowyer, her landlord’s assistant.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:04.809
Bowyer came round to collect the rent and,
even though he was a former soldier, he was

00:13:04.809 --> 00:13:08.920
left stunned by the scene of ineffable horror
that awaited him.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:11.120
First thing he noticed was the broken window.

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:13.709
Inside, the room was absolutely covered in
blood.

00:13:13.709 --> 00:13:18.290
On the table he saw piles of meat, not realizing
in the moment that they were human flesh.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:22.689
On the bed there was the body of Kelly which
had been so grotesquely maimed and mangled

00:13:22.689 --> 00:13:25.350
that it barely looked human anymore.

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:28.579
According to the doctor’s estimation, it
would have taken around two hours to inflict

00:13:28.579 --> 00:13:30.620
those atrocities upon Mary Kelly.

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:34.939
It showed the world just how depraved Jack
the Ripper could be when he had all the time

00:13:34.939 --> 00:13:36.629
and privacy he wanted.

00:13:36.629 --> 00:13:41.220
Police surgeon Dr. Thomas Bond detailed the
extent of her injuries in his report: “The

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:45.569
whole of the surface of the abdomen and thighs
was removed and the abdominal cavity emptied

00:13:45.569 --> 00:13:46.569
of its viscera.

00:13:46.569 --> 00:13:51.209
The breasts were cut off, the arms mutilated
by several jagged wounds and the face hacked

00:13:51.209 --> 00:13:53.089
beyond recognition of the features.

00:13:53.089 --> 00:13:58.180
The tissues of the neck were severed all round
to the bone.”

00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:04.370
The Investigation
On the other side of the law, the London police

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:08.140
force was engaged in one of the most ample
investigations in its history.

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:12.759
Thousands of people were interviewed and hundreds
of leads were chased down, yet police were

00:14:12.759 --> 00:14:16.860
heavily criticized by the public and the media
for failing to apprehend the killer.

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:22.720
The inquiry was initially handled by Whitechapel’s
H Division of the Criminal Investigation Department,

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:25.119
but was soon taken over by Scotland Yard detectives.

00:14:25.119 --> 00:14:30.430
Chief among them was Detective Inspector Frederick
Abberline who was put in charge of the case

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:35.180
because he previously worked for H Division
for 14 years and it was thought that his local

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.050
knowledge would prove invaluable.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:42.209
A frequent criticism throughout the investigation
concerned police refusal to offer a reward

00:14:42.209 --> 00:14:43.499
for information.

00:14:43.499 --> 00:14:47.439
Authorities were accused either of not taking
the case seriously or not caring what happened

00:14:47.439 --> 00:14:50.199
in a poor district full of immigrants like
Whitechapel.

00:14:50.199 --> 00:14:55.279
In reality, this lack of reward was a new
Home Office policy instituted a few years

00:14:55.279 --> 00:14:56.279
earlier.

00:14:56.279 --> 00:14:59.629
If you’re watching this video, you are probably
already aware that the police never caught

00:14:59.629 --> 00:15:00.779
Jack the Ripper.

00:15:00.779 --> 00:15:06.410
That being said, there are two curious moments
in their investigation that are worth discussing.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:08.720
First is a report by surgeon Thomas Bond.

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:12.850
He was asked for his opinion on the killer’s
medical knowledge, but Bond ended up writing

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:17.629
an 11-point essay which is sometimes regarded
as the first ever criminal profile.

00:15:17.629 --> 00:15:22.000
Curiously, Bond vehemently disagreed with
Dr. Phillips’s assertion that Jack the Ripper

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.220
had a medical background.

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:27.550
He didn’t even think the killer had “the
technical knowledge of a butcher or horse

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:28.550
slaughterer.”

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:32.610
Moreover, Bond had no doubt that the five
women were killed “by the same hand.”

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:38.430
He concluded that Jack the Ripper was cool,
daring, middle-aged, quiet, respectably dressed,

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:39.490
and inoffensive looking.

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:43.559
He believed the killer wore a cloak or overcoat
in order to conceal the blood stains after

00:15:43.559 --> 00:15:44.559
the murders.

00:15:44.559 --> 00:15:49.029
Bond said that, in each case, the mutilation
was the Ripper’s main goal and that Jack

00:15:49.029 --> 00:15:54.519
might have suffered from homicidal impulses
brought on by satyriasis, a condition better

00:15:54.519 --> 00:15:58.029
known today as hypersexuality or nymphomania.

00:15:58.029 --> 00:16:02.740
The second moment concerns the only clue that
Jack the Ripper left following a kill.

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:05.279
After he had murdered Catherine Eddowes, he
took her apron.

00:16:05.279 --> 00:16:09.240
Police later found the bloody garment in a
stairwell on Goulston Street.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:13.660
Right above it was a piece of graffiti written
in chalk which read “The Juwes are the men

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.979
that will not be blamed for nothing."

00:16:15.979 --> 00:16:20.079
Police saw it, copied it down and, on the
orders of Police Commissioner Charles Warren,

00:16:20.079 --> 00:16:21.079
wiped it clean.

00:16:21.079 --> 00:16:26.500
At a time of skyhigh racial tensions, he feared
that the text might incite a violent riot.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:30.869
Much debate still goes on regarding whether
the police acted properly by erasing possible

00:16:30.869 --> 00:16:36.149
evidence and whether the graffiti was actually
a message from Jack the Ripper or just a random

00:16:36.149 --> 00:16:40.470
anti-semitic scrawl unconnected to the crimes.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:45.020
More Murders?

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:49.230
The five dead women we have mentioned are
referred to by ripperologists as the Canonical

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:52.820
Five and are, generally, considered Jack’s
only victims.

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:56.779
However, given the uncertainty surrounding
everything else related to the Ripper, it’s

00:16:56.779 --> 00:16:59.550
not surprising that people think he may have
killed others.

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:03.779
First, there were two slayings which took
place in Whitechapel before that of Mary Nichols.The

00:17:03.779 --> 00:17:07.510
first victim was Emma Smith and the second
was Martha Tabram.

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:11.810
Smith survived her attack long enough to tell
police she was assaulted by two or three men,

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:14.760
making it more likely that she fell prey to
gang violence.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.320
Tabram, however, died after being stabbed
39 times.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:22.740
Her kill had the viciousness of Jack the Ripper,
but investigators were, ultimately, convinced

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:28.180
that her death was unrelated because her throat
wasn’t cut and she wasn’t mutilated afterwards.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:32.840
Even so, it wouldn’t be completely unheard
of for a serial killer to evolve his modus

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:38.910
operandi and increase in brutality as he gained
more experience and confidence.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:44.260
Four more suspicious deaths occurred in 1888
and 1889 which were added to the Whitechapel

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:45.260
Murders.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:49.250
However, they were considered unrelated because
they lacked the savage disfigurement of the

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.250
Ripper.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.770
That being said, one of those victims was
just the torso of a woman.

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:57.051
That certainly sounds vicious enough to be
the work of Jack but, as it happened, four

00:17:57.051 --> 00:18:01.570
other torsos had been found around that time,
just not in Whitechapel.

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:06.740
Only one of the victims of the so-called “Thames
Torso Murders” was identified as Elizabeth

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:07.740
Jackson.

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:11.690
Some believe these were all the work of Jack,
while others feel they belonged to a second

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:16.340
maniac who was active at the same time as
the Ripper.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:21.800
Who Was Jack?

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:23.210
Who was Jack the Ripper?

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:28.340
That’s the million dollar question and historians,
scholars, criminologists, authors, and police

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:31.250
officers have put forward over a hundred suspects.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:35.420
Inspector Abberline strongly suspected George
Chapman, a Polish immigrant and a convicted

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:38.280
serial killer who was hanged for three poisonings.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:43.270
Chapman, real name Seweryn Kłosowski, had
minor surgical knowledge and arrived in London

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:45.420
shortly before the killing spree started.

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:49.710
He also left for America in 1891, a few years
after the murders stopped.

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:54.050
However, Chapman used poison and criminologists
don’t believe a killer would change their

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:56.450
modus operandi to such an extent.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:19:00.870
Another convicted serial killer suspected
of being Jack was Dr. Thomas Neill Cream.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:05.260
He was also a poisoner and, according to records,
he was in prison in America during the killing

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.260
spree.

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:10.260
All available evidence should dismiss Cream
as a candidate, yet he remains a popular choice

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:14.990
solely based on the story that, while being
hanged, Cream’s last words allegedly were

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:17.330
“I am Jack…”

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:22.310
A more plausible suspect was Aaron Kosminski,
a Jewish barber who emigrated from Congress

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:24.640
Poland sometime in the early 1880s.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:28.680
He was considered a strong candidate by several
authorities of that era.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:32.850
Sir Melville Macnaghten, Assistant Commissioner
of the London Metropolitan Police, wrote in

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:38.830
memoranda that Kosminski had “strong homicidal
tendencies” and a “great hatred of women,

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.830
especially of the prostitute class.”

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:44.690
Chief Inspector Donald Swanson wrote that
the only witness who got a good look at the

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:49.230
Ripper’s face (doesn’t specify who, but
presumably either Schwartz or Lawende), refused

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:51.510
to testify against him because they were both
Jewish.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:57.410
And although we’re not exactly sure on the
date, sometime around 1890 Kosminski was committed

00:19:57.410 --> 00:20:00.660
to an insane asylum which lines up with the
murders stopping.

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:04.750
Modern science seemingly came to the rescue
when a paper published in the Journal of Forensic

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:10.030
Sciences boldly proclaimed that Aaron Kosminski
was Jack the Ripper based on DNA.

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:15.090
The authors alleged that a semen sample obtained
from the shawl of Catherine Eddowes, the fourth

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:18.090
victim, was DNA matched to a living relative
of Kosminski.

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:22.530
This study, however, was heavily criticized
by other scientists who found many faults

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:23.530
with it.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.660
Even the provenance of the shawl is in doubt.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:30.810
The original inventory done in 1888 lists,
in detail, over 30 items of clothing and possessions

00:20:30.810 --> 00:20:34.840
that Eddowes had on her at the time of her
murder, yet there is no shawl among them.

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:39.620
So while Kosminski remains one of the top
suspects, the matter is yet to be settled.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:45.230
In the same memoranda, Assistant Commissioner
Macnaghten named Montague Druitt as his favored

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:46.230
suspect.

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:50.290
He asserted that Druitt was “sexually insane”
and was suspected of being the Ripper even

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:51.640
by his own family.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:55.650
Druitt committed suicide a month after the
murder of Mary Kelly, giving a reason why

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:56.940
the murders stopped.

00:20:56.940 --> 00:21:01.360
Macnaghten’s appraisal placed Druitt at
the top of the suspect list of many ripperologists,

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:05.590
but it seems to be based mostly on incorrect
facts and hearsay.

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:10.380
Inspector Abberline dismissed Druitt as a
suspect and, decades later, researchers placed

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:13.740
Druitt in different parts of the country for
some of the murders.

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:18.620
Going by viciousness alone, a man named Frederick
Bailey Deeming seemed to be the most likely

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:19.620
culprit.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:23.720
Deeming was hanged in Australia in 1892 for
killing his second wife, only to be later

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:28.120
discovered that he had also murdered his first
wife and their four children by cutting their

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:29.120
throats.

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:32.380
He was certainly capable of inflicting the
gruesome horrors of the Ripper, but records

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:35.370
of his movements in 1888 are spotty, at best.

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:38.950
They seem to indicate that Deeming was in
South Africa at the time.

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:41.780
These are just a few of the more sensible
suspects.

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.290
There are many more out there.

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:48.300
Some believe the killings were the work of
a masonic conspiracy involving the royal family

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:53.170
whose goal was to protect Prince Albert Victor
and that the killer was either the prince

00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:56.790
himself or the Queen’s physician, Sir William
Gull.

00:21:56.790 --> 00:22:02.260
Others opine that the murderer was Lewis Carroll,
author of Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland

00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:05.780
or the post-impressionist painter Walter Sickert.

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:09.500
Some believe that Jack the Ripper was, in
fact, Jill the Ripper, and that the killer

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:10.500
was a woman.

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:13.180
This theory started with Inspector Abberline
himself.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:17.150
Some of the suspects included women of the
era who had been convicted of heinous murders

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:19.880
such as Mary Pearcey and Lizzie Halliday.

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:24.190
We could keep doing this all day and we would
still not run out of suspects.

00:22:24.190 --> 00:22:28.380
Ultimately, there isn’t sufficient evidence
to identify, beyond a shadow of a doubt, any

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:30.500
person as Jack the Ripper.

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:37.150
This anonymity surely helped bolster his infamy
as here we are, 130 years after his ghastly

00:22:37.150 --> 00:22:39.590
killing spree, still talking about it.

00:22:39.590 --> 00:22:44.330
And we are hardly the only ones - books, movies,
and TV shows that revolve around the Ripper

00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:46.100
murders are still popular today.

00:22:46.100 --> 00:23:08.799
So that just leaves us with one question - who
do you think was Jack the Ripper?

